{
  "$comment": "GH-570 - THE LIVE ROWS, COPIED WITH SELECT AND NOT EDITED. Taken from `analysis_results` on the stand on 22.09.2026. They are the input of `Gh569RunCompletenessAsAnEventTest`, so that the rule is judged on the run the owner actually made rather than on a reconstruction of it. `storedOutcome` is what the row says today and is deliberately kept: for id 31 it is the defect itself. It lives under `app/tests/fixtures/` rather than beside the jest fixtures in `tests/fixtures/`, because the application container mounts `./app` and `./assets` and nothing else \u2014 a PHP test cannot read a file the process cannot see.",
  "source": {
    "table": "analysis_results",
    "stand": "local docker (gilba_mysql), database `gilba`",
    "takenAt": "2026-09-22",
    "statement": "SELECT r.id, s.name, r.run_id, r.outcome, r.reason, r.completed_at, r.metrics, r.detail FROM analysis_results r JOIN sites s ON s.id = r.site_id WHERE r.id IN (30, 31, 34)"
  },
